CSCE 4290 – Project 3
Twitter Sentiment Classification Using Word2Vec and Neural Networks
Student Name: Thuan Nguyen
Student ID: 11594515
Course: CSCE 4290
Project: Project 3A and Project 3B

1. Introduction
The objective of this project is to develop a Twitter sentiment classification model using Word2Vec embeddings and a neural network implemented with PyTorch.
The model classifies tweets into three sentiment categories:
Negative (0): Tweets expressing negative opinions or emotions.
Neutral (1): Tweets expressing neither clearly positive nor negative sentiment.
Positive (2): Tweets expressing positive opinions or emotions.
Two experiments were conducted. Project 3A uses frozen pretrained Word2Vec embeddings, while Project 3B allows the pretrained embeddings to be updated during neural network training. The purpose is to compare how fine-tuning word embeddings affects sentiment classification performance.
