The neutral category has the largest number of training examples, while the negative category has the smallest number.
2.2 Text Preprocessing
The following preprocessing steps were applied:
Converted all tweet text to lowercase.
Used regular expressions to tokenize tweets into words and numbers.
Created separate tokenized datasets for training, validation, and testing.
Built a vocabulary using the training tweets.
Added special tokens <PAD> and <UNK> for padding and unknown words.
Converted tweets into numerical sequences.
Truncated sequences longer than 50 tokens and padded shorter sequences to a maximum length of 50.
The resulting vocabulary contained 19,930 entries, including the two special tokens.
