The resulting Word2Vec vocabulary contained 19,928 words. Two additional special tokens were added to create an embedding matrix with a shape of (19,930, 100).
4. Project 3A: Frozen Word2Vec Embeddings
4.1 Model Architecture
Project 3A uses pretrained Word2Vec embeddings with their weights frozen during classifier training.
The model consists of the following components:
An embedding layer initialized with pretrained Word2Vec vectors.
A masked mean pooling operation to calculate the average word embedding for each tweet while ignoring padding tokens.
A fully connected layer with 128 hidden units.
A ReLU activation function.
An output layer with three units representing the sentiment categories.
The embedding layer was configured with freeze=True, meaning its weights remained unchanged during classifier training.
