5. Project 3B: Trainable Word2Vec Embeddings
5.1 Model Architecture
Project 3B uses the same general neural network architecture as Project 3A. However, the pretrained Word2Vec embeddings are trainable.
The embedding layer was configured with freeze=False. Therefore, its weights were updated through backpropagation during neural network training.
The model includes:
A trainable embedding layer initialized with pretrained Word2Vec vectors.
Masked mean pooling to create a tweet representation.
A fully connected layer with 128 hidden units.
A ReLU activation function.
An output layer with three units for sentiment classification.
This approach allows the model to adapt the pretrained word representations to the sentiment classification task.
